  "deductions": [
    "In the tested host, uptake precedes newborn allocation and proposed newborn mass equals 0.12 times current local uptake. This is post-harvest allocation, not preparation that changes the pulse just harvested.",
    "Under fully paid basal costs and uniform turnover tau, a non-reproducing passive tag obeys T_after_h=T_birth*(1-tau)^h. Integer translation cannot change its total. Thus equal-dose tag retention is structurally equal, independently of placement.",
    "Tagged later contact can differ, as can whole-body intake, energy and later birth. Equal tag retention does not make those outcomes equal and does not imply causal mediation by a separate local energy flow.",
    "The preset late pulses insert at most about 0.02 percent of current body mass. These narrow results reject the tested EMA target, not all history-dependent preparation or morphology learning.",
    "The new candidate must act before delayed opportunities are disclosed, incur real preparation cost and affect a subsequent opportunity. This is a task-design hypothesis, not an established new learning method."
